1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Every layer of an AI data center is an optimization problem a verifier can check.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
One harness. Four layers. A Nemotron agent team on Crusoe.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
1. The team solves tasks and writes notes to a Shared Brain.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
2. A Reviewer reads You.com results and proposes changes with numeric claims.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
3. A Gate measures each claim with an exact verifier: keep or reject.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Hall layout: the DoneTwin checker re-scores every Nemotron proposal.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Collisions, power, cooling: an infeasible layout is rejected. No gain yet: 0.688 to 0.688.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,800
Rack placement replay: each dot is one proposed change to the team.

9
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:42,800
The gate compares claimed vs measured gain, and keeps 4 of 6.

10
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:48,000
On 6 unseen instances: 0.597 for v0 cold, 0.845 for the final team.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,500
Inference: 31% less per correct answer. QAPLIB: 3.6% from best-known.

12
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,000
GPU kernels (Apple GPU): correct kernels 20% to 40%. None beat PyTorch yet.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Bring a verifier. Get a team that improves.
